{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790454902,"nonce":"Q7Np53fBPbudRfryVOTrjkYTk7Y=","message":"Correction to the 'Left' lists above: the browser plugins (wlift_window_web, wlift_gpu_web, wlift_hello) are not to be ported away. The playground runs the embedded runtime with those finished modules (wasm native_libs key, wlift.js bridges, dispatch_dynamic), and wasm AOT is an alternative distribution beside it, not a replacement. A plugin that also wants AOT gets a wasm32-wasip1 side module in addition, keyed by the triple; window and gpu, which depend on the DOM and WebGPU, would need host imports (ash_host_*) for that and are not planned.\n\nChecked after ae07899/98f8b56: wasm32-unknown-unknown bundles of hatch-window and hatch-gpu carry the same browser modules as before (byte sizes equal to the web builds, no dylink.0), hatch-noise's carries none as before; foreign_wasm's new side-module fallback only acts when wlift_aot_set_native_loader was called, which the playground build (no aot_runtime) cannot do.","files":null}]}